# inventory (demo target)

A tiny Python inventory library used as the scratch target for Mads-Lens demos.

Run the tests with `pytest`.

## Recent fix

`Inventory.low_stock` in `inventory/core.py` used a strict `<` comparison, so items whose quantity exactly equaled the threshold were left out, contradicting its docstring ("at or below the threshold"). The comparison now uses `<=`, and `test_low_stock_includes_threshold` covers the boundary case.
---
[pytest]
testpaths = tests
---
from dataclasses import dataclass, field


@dataclass
class Item:
    sku: str
    name: str
    price: float
    quantity: int = 0

    def subtotal(self) -> float:
        return self.price * self.quantity


@dataclass
class Inventory:
    items: dict = field(default_factory=dict)

    def add(self, item: Item) -> None:
        if item.sku in self.items:
            self.items[item.sku].quantity += item.quantity
        else:
            self.items[item.sku] = item

    def remove(self, sku: str, quantity: int) -> None:
        if sku not in self.items:
            raise KeyError(sku)
        item = self.items[sku]
        if quantity > item.quantity:
            raise ValueError("not enough stock")
